---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageStyles from '../../components/PageStyles.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Territorial asset management services | Territorium Capital"
  description="Territorium Capital services for landowners, asset managers, companies and institutions: natural capital strategy, climate resilience, restoration, opportunities and measurable territorial projects."
  canonicalPath="/en/services/"
  alternateEsPath="/servicios/"
  lang="en"
>
  <PageStyles />

  <main>
    <section class="services-hero page-first-section reveal">
      <div class="container services-hero__grid">
        <div class="services-hero__copy">
          <span class="section-kicker section-kicker--light">Services</span>
          <h1>Natural capital to manage land better.</h1>
          <p>
            We help public and private landowners, asset managers, companies
            and institutions increase the resilience and profitability of their
            territorial assets through environmental science, proprietary
            technology and execution on the ground.
          </p>
          <div class="services-hero__actions">
            <a href="/contacto/" class="seo-cta seo-cta--solid">Discuss an opportunity</a>
            <a href="/en/projects/" class="seo-cta">View projects</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="services-hero__panel" aria-label="Territorium system">
          <img src="/imagenes/medidas/nuevas/capital-natural-rural.jpg" alt="Rural territory managed as a natural asset">
          <div>
            <span>Territorium system</span>
            <p>
              From ecological and patrimonial reading of the asset to an
              actionable roadmap: manage, regenerate, invest, communicate or
              activate new opportunities.
            </p>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services-operating reveal" aria-label="How we work">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading--left">
          <span class="section-kicker">How we work</span>
          <h2>An operating system for territorial decisions.</h2>
          <p>
            We do not start with an isolated action. We first understand the
            asset, the decision and the economic, environmental or reputational
            objective behind it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="services-operating__grid">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Understand</h3>
            <p>We read biodiversity, water, soil, landscape, risks, uses, constraints and patrimonial potential.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Prioritise</h3>
            <p>We translate data and technical judgement into decisions: what to do, when and with what expected return.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Activate</h3>
            <p>We design resilience, restoration, opportunity, nature-positive or preventive management projects.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>04</span>
            <h3>Measure</h3>
            <p>We turn progress into evidence: indicators, monitoring, baselines and responsible communication.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services-capabilities reveal" aria-label="Territorium capabilities">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading--left">
          <span class="section-kicker">Capabilities</span>
          <h2>One logic for value, resilience and profitability.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="services-capabilities__grid">
          <a class="services-capability" href="/valor-ecologico-territorio/">
            <img src="/imagenes/servicio-diagnostico-capas.png" alt="Territorial analysis with environmental layers">
            <div>
              <span>01</span>
              <h3>Diagnosis and ecological value</h3>
              <p>Measure the condition of the territory and understand what natural, patrimonial and strategic value it can activate.</p>
            </div>
          </a>

          <a class="services-capability" href="/en/projects/ecological-restoration-living-lab/">
            <img src="/imagenes/medidas/nuevas/biodiversidad-ciervo.jpg" alt="Wildlife as a biodiversity indicator">
            <div>
              <span>02</span>
              <h3>Evidence and ecological monitoring</h3>
              <p>Baselines, indicators and continuous measurement to demonstrate real improvement, not just intention.</p>
            </div>
          </a>

          <a class="services-capability" href="/proyectos/resiliencia-agricola/">
            <img src="/imagenes/medidas/nuevas/riesgo-climatico-sequia.jpg" alt="Agricultural territory affected by drought">
            <div>
              <span>03</span>
              <h3>Climate and agricultural resilience</h3>
              <p>Analyse how soil, water, vegetation and biodiversity reduce vulnerability to climate events.</p>
            </div>
          </a>

          <a class="services-capability" href="/en/opportunities/">
            <img src="/imagenes/medidas/nuevas/paisaje-spain.jpg" alt="Rural landscape assessed for opportunities">
            <div>
              <span>04</span>
              <h3>Opportunities and profitability</h3>
              <p>Match asset data with funding calls, incentives and financing pathways that genuinely fit.</p>
            </div>
          </a>

          <a class="services-capability" href="/proyectos/viviendas-impacto-positivo/">
            <img src="/imagenes/territorio-urbano-analisis.jpg" alt="Green infrastructure analysis in an urban environment">
            <div>
              <span>05</span>
              <h3>Nature-positive impact</h3>
              <p>Apply reduction, avoidance, on-site improvement and off-site restoration logic to transformative projects.</p>
            </div>
          </a>

          <a class="services-capability" href="/proyectos/sistema-alerta-temprana-arbolado/">
            <img src="/imagenes/medidas/nuevas/conectividad-bosque.jpg" alt="Forest and trees as natural infrastructure">
            <div>
              <span>06</span>
              <h3>Early warning and preventive management</h3>
              <p>Monitoring systems to anticipate risks, prioritise inspections and act before incidents occur.</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="seo-section seo-section--white reveal">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <span class="section-kicker">Applications</span>
          <h2>From rural asset to corporate project.</h2>
          <p>
            Territorium works where land needs to become a decision:
            patrimonial management, climate resilience, natural capital
            investment, measurable restoration or evidence-based communication.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="seo-card-grid seo-card-grid--four">
          <article class="seo-card">
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Landowners and managers</h3>
            <p>Increase resilience, profitability and patrimonial value with a clear territorial roadmap.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="seo-card">
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Companies</h3>
            <p>Build local, traceable and measurable projects linked to nature, climate and territory.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="seo-card">
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Developers and institutions</h3>
            <p>Integrate biodiversity, water, soil and restoration into project decisions and positive impact.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="seo-card">
            <span>04</span>
            <h3>Families and investors</h3>
            <p>Evaluate assets, risks and opportunities linked to land, resilience and natural capital.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services-final-cta reveal">
      <div class="container services-final-cta__inner">
        <span class="section-kicker section-kicker--light">Next step</span>
        <h2>Defining the scope well avoids weak projects.</h2>
        <p>
          Tell us what decision you need to make: improve a land asset,
          structure a corporate project, measure resilience or identify
          profitability opportunities linked to territory.
        </p>
        <a href="/contacto/" class="seo-cta seo-cta--solid">Talk to Territorium</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries, currentObserver) => {
      entries.forEach(entry => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("active");
          currentObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.1 });
    document.querySelectorAll(".reveal").forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
  });
</script>
